The diagram shows three curves. Which curve is $y=\log_{3}x$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-4,xmax=8,ymin=-4,ymax=8,xtick={-4,-2,2,4,6,8},ytick={-4,-2,2,4,6,8},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,red!70!black,dashdotted,<->,domain=0.0123:7.9,samples=100] {ln(x)/ln(3)};
\node[red!70!black] at (axis cs:7,2.4) {$A$};
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-3.5:1.9,samples=100] {exp(x*ln(3))};
\node[blue!70!black] at (axis cs:2.3,6.8) {$B$};
\addplot[thick,green!50!black,densely dashed,<->,domain=0.0123:7.9,samples=100] {ln(x)/ln(0.3333)};
\node[green!50!black] at (axis cs:7,-2.4) {$C$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

