A logarithmic curve $y=\log_{a}x$ passes through $(1,0)$ and $(9,2)$. What is the base $a$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-1,xmax=10,ymin=-4,ymax=4,xtick={2,4,6,8},ytick={-4,-2,2,4},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=0.0123:9.5,samples=100] {ln(x)/ln(3)};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,mark size=2pt] coordinates {(1,0) (9,2)};
\node[below right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (axis cs:1,0) {$(1,0)$};
\node[above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (axis cs:9,2) {$(9,2)$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
